WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.613
The same deck can feel like a product launch, a quiet documentary, or a punchy social clip.

2
00:00:06.663 --> 00:00:08.705
It all depends on how it moves.

3
00:00:09.205 --> 00:00:11.129
Your content stays yours.

4
00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:18.352
The look changes the framing, the motion, how text arrives, where captions sit, and the overall texture.

5
00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:21.495
These are directions, not presets.

6
00:00:21.545 --> 00:00:23.794
Clean and corporate suits training.

7
00:00:23.844 --> 00:00:26.952
Calm and cinematic suits brand stories.

8
00:00:27.002 --> 00:00:30.425
Bold and energetic competes for attention in a feed.

9
00:00:30.925 --> 00:00:33.092
Three questions narrow it down.

10
00:00:33.142 --> 00:00:34.857
Where will people watch?

11
00:00:34.907 --> 00:00:36.889
What one word should they feel?

12
00:00:36.939 --> 00:00:39.663
And how much text is on your slides?

13
00:00:39.713 --> 00:00:42.846
Denser slides need a clean or calm direction.

14
00:00:43.346 --> 00:00:47.697
On your launch page, the headline gets slow, confident movement.

15
00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:51.714
Cut to three slides for social, and it becomes: Scheduling.

16
00:00:51.764 --> 00:00:52.503
Sorted.

17
00:00:52.553 --> 00:00:54.502
Same brand, two videos.

18
00:00:55.002 --> 00:00:57.472
Decide the direction, then see it.

19
00:00:57.522 --> 00:01:02.197
On Pro, AI directs your video, shaping each scene to your tone.

20
00:01:02.247 --> 00:01:07.179
Try Basic first, no subscription needed, at powerpoint2vid.com.

